nd a  dq ice cream cake that i need to enjoy  this summer  so thank you very much dairy gods  and i'm also tolerating like moderate  amounts of fodmaps as well  now i have admittedly made an effort to  really cut back on like my salad intake  so i'm eating most of my vegetables  either in like a smoothie but mainly  like a cooked vegetable side dish  but i have found that even on the  occasion that i have had a little salad  at dinner  it hasn't caused the same level of  bloating  at nighttime like it had been before so  this is promising this is feeling  good and this is really gross oh my gosh  yeah i think we'll probably do a retest  after i'm done nursing just to see where  i'm netting out and see if there's any  additional improvements that maybe could  be made  with another course of antibiotics but  until then i'm feeling good so i guess  this video is  tbd and maybe in the fall we can pick  this back up with another leg of this  journey  and maybe just maybe  i can ease off some of the restrictions  and supplements  it'll be really nice to be able to be a  little bit more flexible with my eating  and snacking schedule throughout the day  but i guess for now i will just kind of  relish in a sweet little victory  that is being able to tolerate dairy  again  ben jerry's get at me boys  and on that note another big thank you  to my colleagues andrea hardy aaron  judge  and ali coogler for helping me navigate  this topic  and answering some of my questions as  they are the experts in this field  again i'm going to leave their contacts  below in case you're interested in  getting some more one-on-one advice  and hearing more about what they can  offer and on that note if you like this  video be sure to give it  the thumbs up leave me a comment below  on any other vlog content or topics you  want me to make a video about  subscribe to the channel and i'll see  you next time on abby's kitchen  bye and for more great videos like this  check out the link right here  y